THOUGHT: The NullAway errors in SpriteDrawable come from dereferencing a @Nullable sprite field without checks. The simplest fix is to enforce non-null in setSprite by throwing if null is passed, and then remove @Nullable from the parameter and getter so NullAway knows sprite is always non-null after construction. I’ll update setSprite to reject null and adjust annotations accordingly.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '83,91c\  public void setSprite(Sprite sprite) {
    if (sprite == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("sprite cannot be null.");
    this.sprite = sprite;
    setMinWidth(sprite.getWidth());
    setMinHeight(sprite.getHeight());
  }

  public Sprite getSprite() {
    return sprite;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/utils/SpriteDrawable.java
```

